From 8bc015f8ffa6ba9dbf3c420cbe1446009039f99e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler South <tsouth2@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 23:06:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Deliver pinch touchpad rules to existing guests

Persistent disks created before the pinch device never received its rules file or the loader in input.lua. Revision 34 delivers the rules through the compat overlay, and catch-up appends a guarded loader to each user's input.lua once, keeping the original as input.lua.before-try-omarchy-pinch. The loader only runs dofile when the rules file exists, so input.lua no longer breaks after try-omarchy-export copies it to a real Omarchy install; the unguarded line earlier images added is replaced. Symlinked files, files ending in a top-level return, and a user's own device rule are left alone.

A udev rule makes libinput ignore the device until try-omarchy-pinch-ready confirms at each boot that every desktop user's Hyprland config loads the rules, so a guest that could not be migrated keeps ordinary input without stray tap clicks. The reason is written to /run/try-omarchy/pinch-gestures.
